---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PortfolioScene from "../components/PortfolioScene.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Portfolio"
  description="Portfolio of Alonza Blanding Jr. — cybersecurity and OSINT analyst working in open source intelligence and counter-trafficking."
>
  <section class="portfolio-hero">
    <PortfolioScene />
    <h1>Alonza Blanding Jr.</h1>
    <p class="portfolio-subtitle">Cybersecurity / OSINT Analyst</p>
    <p>
      Open source intelligence practitioner working toward mission-driven
      analyst work — researching in the open, writing about what I learn,
      and aiming those skills at the fight against human trafficking.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>About</h2>
    <p>
      I started in telecom customer care, where I learned to listen for
      patterns — the pause before a lie, the account that didn't add up, the
      voice asking for help without asking. That instinct became OSINT. I
      went back to school, earned my degree in Information Technology with
      a specialization in Information Assurance and Cybersecurity, and
      began building toward analyst work that supports law enforcement
      against traffickers and predators.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Certifications</h2>
    <ul class="portfolio-list">
      <li><strong>Practical OSINT Research Professional (PORP)</strong> — TCM Security</li>
      <li><strong>Google IT Support</strong> — Google</li>
      <li><strong>Practical Help Desk Associate (PHDA)</strong> — TCM Security, in progress</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Experience</h2>
    <ul class="portfolio-list">
      <li>
        <strong>Expert, Loyalty — T-Mobile</strong> (2025–present; previously Technical Expert, 2024–2025)
        <br />Customer care and technical support in a high-volume call center environment.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Volunteer OSINT Analyst — Skull Games Task Force</strong> (since October 2026)
        <br />Volunteer analyst supporting counter-trafficking operations.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>OSINT Intern — The OSINT Insider</strong> (since September 2026)
        <br />Internship work where OSINT meets journalism.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Global OSINT Search Party CTF Participant — Trace Labs</strong> (August 2026)
        <br />Competitive open source intelligence event focused on finding missing persons.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Projects</h2>
    <ul class="portfolio-list">
      <li>
        <strong><a href="/blog">OSINT Journey blog</a></strong>
        <br />Ongoing writing on OSINT research, certifications, CTFs, and counter-trafficking — what I learn, what I get wrong, and how I improve.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>OSINT research and writing</strong>
        <br />General open source research, methodology notes, and book and course reviews.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      The best place to reach me professionally is
      <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/alonza-blanding-124876118">LinkedIn</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
